    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the shared-household feature so that `sharesHousehold=true` both waives the duplicate-household rejection *and* assigns a stable, shared `householdId`, returning it on the owner.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a `householdId` field mapped to a new `household_id` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schema** \u2014 added the `household_id` column to the owners table in all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and it's returned by `GET`/`POST`.\n\n4. **New `Households` component** (`rest/controller`) \u2014 the single home for household *identity*: normalization (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed last name + address), `findMembers(candidate)`, and `stableId(candidate)` (a deterministic UUID derived from the household key, so the same household always yields the same id).\n\n5. **`HouseholdDuplicateValidator`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `Households.findMembers`, removing the duplicated normalization/matching logic it previously carried.\n\n6. **New `HouseholdAssigner` component** \u2014 implements the join: computes the stable `householdId`, sets it on the new owner, and back-fills it onto matching existing members (so \"both\" carry the same id). No-op when no existing owner shares the household.\n\n7. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 now branches: `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 `householdAssigner.assignSharedHousehold(owner)` (before persist); otherwise the duplicate guard runs as before.\n\n8. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 `householdId` maps entity\u2192DTO automatically; ignored on the fields\u2192entity mapping (it's derived, not client-supplied), matching the existing `id`/`pets`/`customerCode` pattern.\n\nEach responsibility lives in its own small unit \u2014 matching/identity in `Households`, rejection in the validator, assignment in the assigner \u2014 and the shared logic is reused rather than copied.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` passes: two owners joining the same address/last name receive an identical, non-blank `householdId`.",
